Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal, bubblewrap
Suggests: libgtk-layer-shell0, appimagetool
Description: Run a single .hta file as a Linux desktop application
 HTML App turns one HTML file into a first-class Linux desktop application, with a
 capability model that makes that safe. No build step, no bundler, no project
 directory: the input is a file, not a project.
 .
 A document with no manifest gets no native APIs at all. Everything else is declared
 in the document, enforced in Rust, and pinned to the file's content hash, so editing
 a file asks again.
